{"kind":"article","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Explicit equality guards (","type":"text"},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are unnecessary. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already checks equality on ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2},{"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc: